{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And you shall say to Pharaoh.</b> When you hear that his heart is stubborn and he refuses to send, say this to him:" "<b>My son, My firstborn.</b> A term of greatness; as in ״אַף אֲנִי בְּכוֹר אֶתְנֶהוּ״ (Psalms 89) — this is its plain sense. And its midrash: here the Holy One, blessed be He, set His seal upon the recognition of the birthright that Jacob took from Esau (Bereshit Rabbah 63)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:32.764651884Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}